validated\nfor ProgramRule/ProgramRuleAction: the redundant-put/contention mechanism\nthat motivated removing Option's L2 cache entirely is specific to\nNONSTRICT_READ_WRITE's putFromLoad (AbstractCachedDomainDataAccess -- always\nputs unconditionally, no cache-presence check at all). READ_WRITE's\nputFromLoad (AbstractReadWriteAccess) skips the put when the item is\nalready cache-resident, for any non-versioned entity -- confirmed against\nthe actual Hibernate 5.6.15 jar in use. Option/OptionSet are non-versioned\nand confirmed never written in this workload (rare admin edits only), so\nREAD_WRITE's soft-lock forced-miss downside (which only engages on a\nconcurrent write) costs almost nothing here, while its put-skip should\neliminate the concurrency-scaling redundant-put cost without sacrificing\nthe ~99.97%-hit-ratio free keyed-lookup benefit that full removal threw\naway.\n\nRestores class-level caches on Option and OptionSet, the OptionSet.options\ncollection cache, and the three named ehcache.xml regions (OptionSet,\nOptionSet.options, Option) that were dropped as dead config when caching\nwas removed. batch-size=\"100\" on Option is left in place as defense-in-depth\nfor cold-cache/eviction bursts.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","author":{"name":"Jason Pickering","email":"jason@dhis2.org"},"id":"025cf5afbed07ad3a762d8a452815f5566721753","tree_id":"de743657bb0cbc0b20d468747403a62042a5cb95","timestamp":"2026-08-06T07:15:28Z","committer":{"name":"Jason Pickering","email":"jason@dhis2.org"}},"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/workflows/10954","repository":{"id":66940520,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk2Njk0MDUyMA==","owner":{"login":"dhis2","id":1089987,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjEwODk5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1089987?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2","gravatar_id":"","type":"Organization","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/user